course: dictionary
lesson: 7534
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «Preach» can mean giving a religious talk in church. «Jonah preached, and the whole city of Nineveh said sorry.» People saying sorry after a talk tells you preached means speaking to people about God.
explain: The second meaning is to tell others strongly that something is right. «Preach kindness» means to speak strongly about how important kindness is. Try swapping in «talk strongly about» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: The third meaning is informal and often shows disapproval. «Stop preaching at me!» sounds cross, so preaching means giving advice in an annoying, bossy way. Notice the tone of voice: the feeling in a sentence is a clue too.
fact: Preach is a verb: preach, preaches, preached, preaching.
fact: «Preach» means to give a religious talk, called a sermon, usually in a church.
fact: «Preach» can also mean to tell others strongly that something is right.
fact: Informal «preach» means to lecture people in an annoying, bossy way.
fact: «Practise what you preach» means do what you tell others to do.
exercise: «Jonah preached, and the whole city of Nineveh said sorry.» What does preached mean here? | Sang loudly in the street | Ran away on a ship | *Gave a religious talk to the people | Fell into the sea
exercise: The speaker says crossly, «Stop preaching at me!» What does preaching mean here? | Singing a hymn | Giving a church sermon | Painting a picture | *Giving bossy advice in an annoying way
exercise: What does «practise what you preach» mean? | *Do what you tell others to do | Practise a sermon at home every day | Never tell anyone what to do | Only talk about church
test: What does «preach kindness» mean? | To run away from trouble | To sing a hymn in church | To lecture about maths homework | *To tell others strongly that kindness is right
test: Which word is the past tense of preach? | praised | *preached | prayed | preacher
exam: Someone says, «You're preaching to the converted.» What does it mean? | They want you to sing | They are about to leave the room | They have never heard of the idea | *They already agree with what you are saying
